501
00:20:28,362 --> 00:20:30,363
- You're a man playing
a woman playing a man.

502
00:20:30,397 --> 00:20:33,967
- ...out of business
and liquidate the inventory

503
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,068
and the other assets

504
00:20:35,102 --> 00:20:37,703
and then use that money
to buy the next place.

505
00:20:37,737 --> 00:20:38,972
- You're brilliant.

506
00:20:39,005 --> 00:20:40,840
- Oh, it's just not possible.

507
00:20:40,873 --> 00:20:42,108
- Tell that to Dave Del Dotto.

508
00:20:42,142 --> 00:20:44,310
- Have you noticed how
that line of property lies?

509
00:20:44,343 --> 00:20:45,578
- Don't you hate that?

510
00:20:45,612 --> 00:20:47,913
- You said it looked
like a geometric pattern.

511
00:20:47,948 --> 00:20:50,550
Well, picture it
in your mind's eye.

512
00:20:50,583 --> 00:20:53,053
- Well, I get it,
it's funny.

513
00:20:53,087 --> 00:20:54,387
- Yeah. Oh, yeah.
I see it now.

514
00:20:54,420 --> 00:20:55,755
- Yeah, baby,
that's real, yeah.

515
00:20:55,788 --> 00:20:57,757
- It lies on the ground
that the Land Commission

516
00:20:57,790 --> 00:20:59,627
has picked out
as a suggested right-of-way

517
00:20:59,660 --> 00:21:01,728
for the railroad and depot.

518
00:21:01,762 --> 00:21:02,928
- Exactly.

519
00:21:02,963 --> 00:21:03,930
- You mean, I am right?

520
00:21:03,963 --> 00:21:05,298
- Oh, but Erica,
this scheme of yours

521
00:21:05,332 --> 00:21:08,802
is the height of
speculative gambling.

522
00:21:08,835 --> 00:21:10,870
The railroad decides
not to build through Oracle,

523
00:21:10,903 --> 00:21:11,872
you'll be wiped out.

524
00:21:11,905 --> 00:21:12,905
- [indistinct].

525
00:21:12,938 --> 00:21:14,642
- It's a chance.

526
00:21:14,675 --> 00:21:16,610
- An extremely long one.

527
00:21:16,643 --> 00:21:19,445
- Well, I got to hit my shift
at Road Rogers.

528
00:21:19,478 --> 00:21:21,982
- Well, I want those trains
to come through, too,

529
00:21:22,015 --> 00:21:23,550
and I guess
we'll get the decision

530
00:21:23,583 --> 00:21:25,985
in Saturday's
postal express.

531
00:21:27,453 --> 00:21:30,157
'Course you realize
how the town'll feel if...

532
00:21:30,190 --> 00:21:32,525
- Some nights I lie awake
two or three seconds

533
00:21:32,558 --> 00:21:33,527
worrying about it.

534
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:34,527
- Oops, sorry.

535
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:36,763
- Goodnight, Mayor.

536
00:21:36,797 --> 00:21:41,133
- Goodnight, Erica,
and good luck.

537
00:21:41,167 --> 00:21:42,668
- Thanks for the drinks
and stuff.

538
00:21:42,702 --> 00:21:45,272
Sorry, I was such the pig
with a chex mix.

539
00:21:46,507 --> 00:21:48,942
- So, it's like he's been in
the little men's room there.

540
00:21:48,975 --> 00:21:52,812
- ...Tombstone.
Got the man you wanted.

541
00:21:52,845 --> 00:21:54,647
I got the best.

542
00:21:54,682 --> 00:21:56,015
- What's his name?

543
00:21:56,048 --> 00:21:57,183
- Cane Miro.

544
00:22:06,427 --> 00:22:07,993
- Rum, dum, dum.

545
00:22:08,028 --> 00:22:10,297
dum, dum, dum, dum...

546
00:22:10,330 --> 00:22:12,565
- So, this is what
it's like to be dead.

547
00:22:12,598 --> 00:22:15,435
- Well, roughly this is what
it's like to be in a casket.

548
00:22:15,468 --> 00:22:17,503
- So, why are we doing this?

549
00:22:17,537 --> 00:22:18,738
- Aren't you curious?

550
00:22:18,772 --> 00:22:20,040
- About being dead?

551
00:22:20,073 --> 00:22:21,240
We're robots, Joel.

552
00:22:21,273 --> 00:22:22,742
We're not the ones
who have to worry about it,

553
00:22:22,775 --> 00:22:24,210
you understand my point.

554
00:22:24,243 --> 00:22:25,978
- Oh, yeah, well, at least
I have a soul, okay.

555
00:22:26,012 --> 00:22:27,113
- Yeah, sure you do.

556
00:22:27,147 --> 00:22:28,815
Anyway, even though
I'm not going to die,

557
00:22:28,848 --> 00:22:30,983
I sure could see having
a snappy funeral.

558
00:22:31,017 --> 00:22:32,652
- Not like the one
in the movie though.

559
00:22:32,685 --> 00:22:33,787
What a drag!

560
00:22:33,820 --> 00:22:34,822
- Oh, at my funeral,

561
00:22:34,855 --> 00:22:36,457
I'd hope my friends
would toss me up and down

562
00:22:36,490 --> 00:22:38,525
in a blanket like
the Eskimos do, you know?

563
00:22:38,558 --> 00:22:39,592
Really go for some height.

564
00:22:39,625 --> 00:22:40,860
- Well, how about
a beach funeral?

565
00:22:40,893 --> 00:22:42,695
You know, pony cake, bonfire,

566
00:22:42,728 --> 00:22:45,365
couple slipping off
into the woods to neck.

567
00:22:45,398 --> 00:22:47,067
Brought me up
so I can serve.

568
00:22:47,100 --> 00:22:49,035
- Hey, I'd go
the dignity route.

569
00:22:49,068 --> 00:22:50,803
You know,
variety of ethnic foods

570
00:22:50,837 --> 00:22:53,073
or maybe a saxophone quartet.

571
00:22:53,107 --> 00:22:54,373
- Dignity, smagnity, Joel.

572
00:22:54,407 --> 00:22:55,808
I want elephants,
lots of them,

573
00:22:55,842 --> 00:22:58,112
and circus ladies
as my pallbearers.

574
00:22:58,145 --> 00:22:59,412
I want them enthusiastic

575
00:22:59,445 --> 00:23:02,382
and wearing those little frilly
skirts as little tutus.

576
00:23:02,415 --> 00:23:05,085
- You know, Tom Cross
could be a consideration.

577
00:23:05,118 --> 00:23:06,352
- Nonsense, Joel.

578
00:23:06,385 --> 00:23:08,088
I'll lie in state
for several days

579
00:23:08,122 --> 00:23:10,057
at the Corn Palace
while Hooked On a Feeling

580
00:23:10,090 --> 00:23:12,092
sung by a choir of castrati.

581
00:23:12,125 --> 00:23:14,227
- You know, there's always
the educational route,

582
00:23:14,227 --> 00:23:15,928
so a real hands-on
kind of funeral,

583
00:23:15,962 --> 00:23:19,032
details of my embalming
written up and distributed.

584
00:23:19,065 --> 00:23:21,033
- It is fun to think about it.

585
00:23:21,067 --> 00:23:23,068
- That sure is.

586
00:23:23,103 --> 00:23:26,740
So, when you humans die,
that's it, right,

587
00:23:26,773 --> 00:23:27,873
you're dead forever?

588
00:23:27,907 --> 00:23:28,942
- Yeah.

589
00:23:28,975 --> 00:23:30,110
- Well, isn't that like
throwing the baby out

590
00:23:30,143 --> 00:23:31,445
with the bath water, Joel?

591
00:23:31,478 --> 00:23:33,813
- Why don't you just
not die, Joel?

592
00:23:33,847 --> 00:23:35,015
- Well, everybody dies.

593
00:23:35,048 --> 00:23:38,083
- And if everybody ran
off a cliff, you'd do that too.

594
00:23:38,118 --> 00:23:39,853
- Well, that's not the way
it works,

595
00:23:39,887 --> 00:23:41,722
besides
we got commercial sign.

596
00:23:41,755 --> 00:23:43,423
- That's just weird,
that's all.

597
00:23:43,457 --> 00:23:44,858
- Maybe it's us.

598
00:23:44,892 --> 00:23:46,627
Joel, is there any way
I could be mummified

599
00:23:46,660 --> 00:23:48,262
and placed next to Stalin?

600
00:23:48,295 --> 00:23:49,428
- Sure, honey.

601
00:23:49,462 --> 00:23:50,663
- That's what I want,

602
00:23:50,697 --> 00:23:53,733
mummified and placed
next to Stalin.

603
00:23:53,767 --> 00:23:55,568
- [HUMMING]
♪ Rum dum dum ♪

604
00:23:55,602 --> 00:23:58,103
♪ Dum dum dum dum... ♪

605
00:24:00,573 --> 00:24:03,543
[♪♪♪]

606
00:24:07,447 --> 00:24:08,682
- Death sucks.

607
00:24:10,317 --> 00:24:13,052
- Yeah, I don't even want
to know what I stepped in.

608
00:24:15,188 --> 00:24:17,190
- Sheepers, it's hard
to get into this town.

609
00:24:17,223 --> 00:24:18,958
- Stop it, Mister.
I've got you cold.

610
00:24:18,992 --> 00:24:20,827
- Yeah, she does.

611
00:24:25,498 --> 00:24:26,700
- Say.

612
00:24:26,733 --> 00:24:28,635
- Whaddya know?

613
00:24:28,668 --> 00:24:29,903
A lady with a star.

614
00:24:29,937 --> 00:24:32,538
- ♪ You can dust your car
To the lady with the star ♪

615
00:24:32,572 --> 00:24:34,473
- You're not the man
I'm after.

616
00:24:34,507 --> 00:24:36,275
- I'm sorry.
- I'm really sorry.

617
00:24:36,308 --> 00:24:37,943
- I'm sorry
I took a shot at you.

618
00:24:37,977 --> 00:24:40,047
- That's one on me.
- My name's Rose Hood.

619
00:24:40,080 --> 00:24:41,815
- Cane Miro.
- Cane Miro?

620
00:24:41,848 --> 00:24:43,750
- Any relation to John Miro?

621
00:24:43,783 --> 00:24:45,485
- Well, that sounds familiar.

622
00:24:45,518 --> 00:24:47,320
- I don't think we've met.

623
00:24:47,353 --> 00:24:49,655
If we had,
I'd have remembered.

624
00:24:49,688 --> 00:24:51,625
- I'm the Marshal here.
I'm glad I missed you.

625
00:24:51,658 --> 00:24:53,793
I was aiming at a killer
I mean to catch.

626
00:24:53,827 --> 00:24:54,862
- There he goes now.

627
00:24:54,895 --> 00:24:56,362
- I'd like to help you, ma'am.

628
00:24:56,395 --> 00:24:58,298
- Well, he's supposed to be
hiding out in Nine Mile Canyon.

629
00:24:58,332 --> 00:25:00,067
- How long is that canyon?

630
00:25:00,100 --> 00:25:01,602
- As a matter of fact,
I did see some smoke

631
